w: Now, my soul, thy voice up- rais- ing, Tell in sweet and mourn- ful strain
w: Scourged with un- re- lent- ing fu- ry For the sins which we de- plore,
w: See! His hands and feet are fast- ened! So He makes His peo- ple free;
w: Through His heart the spear is pierc- ing, Though His foes have seen Him die;
w: Je- su, may those pre- cious foun- tains Drink to thirst- ing souls af- ford:
